# 2. Extraction criteria and utility. 1:00.
s=new("Nuwa turns mental models into rules an agent can apply",n=2,
      source="Nuwa core + extraction framework @7812110. Examples paraphrase the repo's Karpathy skill. AI4R uses are proposals.",
      notes=note("TIME 1:00. A mental model is a reusable lens, while a decision rule tells the agent what to do in a particular situation. Nuwa keeps three to seven models. Each must recur across at least two domains, generate judgments on new questions, and distinguish the person's perspective from generic advice. A qualifying model needs supporting scenes, an application and a limitation. Decision heuristics are concrete if-then rules, typically five to ten, with case evidence. The Karpathy example links understanding through construction to rebuilding a minimal core, and contains a data-inspection-before-training rule. We paraphrase the repository's extracted skill here, not independently verified personal statements. Nuwa also records tensions and derives factual research directions from the models. AI4R could imitate this separation of a rationale, an executable step, its evidence requirements and its failure conditions. These qualitative filters select useful candidates; they do not validate scientific correctness.","core","framework","karpathy","template"))
table(s,0.7,1.62,[2.05,3.25,3.7,2.9],[
    ["What Nuwa extracts","Example from the skill","Nuwa's retention criterion","Utility to AI4R"],
    ["Mental models\n3–7 lenses","Understanding through construction","Recurs in at least 2 domains, generates new judgments, and is distinctive","Reusable strategy with an explicit rationale"],
    ["Decision rules\n5–10 heuristics","Before training a model, inspect the data","A concrete if-then rule with a supporting case","Executable investigation steps"],
    ["Limits and tensions","Deep reconstruction can conflict with speed","Keep counterexamples, scope limits and changes over time","Applicability and failure conditions"],
    ["Research directions","For reliability claims, inspect tail failures","Derive specific evidence questions from the models","Tool use driven by evidence needs"]],size=16.5,rh=0.97)
shape(s,MSO_SHAPE.RECTANGLE,0.7,6.16,11.9,0.4,fill=ORANGE_L)
put(s.shapes[-1],"AI4R can reuse the reasoning procedure while keeping a neutral research voice.",size=17,bold=True,color=TERRA)

# 3. Source exploration and research criteria. 1:05.
s=new("Nuwa researches six views of the person",n=3,
      source="Nuwa SKILL.md, Phase 1 @7812110. A host agent executes these research instructions and saves each stream.",
      notes=note("TIME 1:05. A name and target trait first define the scope. The host agent then researches six views of the person. Writings reveal recurring arguments, interviews reveal reasoning under pressure, and short-form expression reveals voice. Criticism provides counterexamples, decisions test statements against actions, and the timeline records change. Each stream saves research with source and confidence, distinguishing direct statements, outside reports and inference. Nuwa prefers primary material, including supplied local sources, and retains unresolved contradictions. If the user provides a strong corpus, it searches only for missing dimensions. Its later quality targets include more than half primary sources, specific model limits, honest boundaries and tensions. Finally, it checks known positions, an unfamiliar question and recognizable voice. AI4R can learn to collect evidence that challenges a candidate rule and retain its provenance, rather than generate a polished method from a few quotations. These are prescribed criteria, not proof that every example meets them.","core","framework","rubric"))
text(s,0.7,1.15,11.9,0.35,"Six parallel research agents, with serial fallback. Each stream saves a sourced research file.",size=17,color=TERRA,align="l",inset=0)
table(s,0.7,1.62,[2.05,3.5,3.35,3.0],[
    ["Research stream","Where it explores","What it tries to establish","AI4R lesson"],
    ["Writings","Books, essays, papers, newsletters","Claims repeated at least 3 times; original concepts","Stable candidate principles"],
    ["Conversations","Long interviews, podcasts, AMA","Reasoning under questions and changing positions","Decision process beyond quotes"],
    ["Expression","Posts and short-form writing","Vocabulary, rhythm, certainty and humor","Separate voice from method"],
    ["Outside views","Criticism, biographies, peer accounts","Blind spots and counterexamples","Adversarial evidence"],
    ["Decisions","Major choices, actions and outcomes","Whether behavior supports stated beliefs","Rules grounded in cases"],
    ["Timeline","Milestones and recent developments","When views changed and what is current","Version and refresh conditions"]],size=16,rh=0.65)
shape(s,MSO_SHAPE.RECTANGLE,0.7,6.1,11.9,0.55,fill=ORANGE_L)
put(s.shapes[-1],["Sources: primary material first, with confidence, contradictions and inference labels.","Checks: 3 known positions, 1 unfamiliar case and voice. Target: over 50% primary sources."],size=16,bold=True,color=TERRA)

# 4. Concrete example with the person retained. 0:45.
s=new("Example: a Karpathy skill challenges an agent benchmark",n=4,
      source="Karpathy perspective example @7812110. The research question and response below are illustrative framework inferences.",
      notes=note("TIME 0:45. Take the Karpathy perspective included in the repository. Its documented lenses include the gap between a demo and reliable deployment, difficult tail cases, and learning from real implementations. Suppose an AI4Research agent sees a paper claiming a highly reliable research assistant. A procedure derived from those lenses would ask which task distribution the benchmark covers, what happens in a long run when tools fail, and which evidence can be reproduced. This shows how a model becomes research questions. The response is our illustration derived from the skill, not a quotation or a claim about Karpathy's view of a particular paper. These questions may also arise from a generic checklist. Added value over a generic reviewer is untested, which is why that comparator belongs in the trial.","karpathy"))
